    {
      "id": 300,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "3 · What drives the bytes",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 43,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 301,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 44,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Shows:** event-query bytes split by query shape (selector, whether it is time-bounded, whether payloads are filtered), how many polls were answered with 304 Not Modified, and how much gzip saves. **Healthy:** bytes per query stays flat as history grows; the 304 share rises as clients send `If-None-Match`; wire/raw sits well under 100%. **Act when:** an unbounded or unfiltered shape dominates. That client re-reads history it already has. The gzip ratio counts every event-query response, including clients that did not ask for gzip."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 302,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Event-query bytes by shape",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 47,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{selector}} · bounded={{time_bounded}} · filtered={{payload_filtered}}",
          "expr": "sum by (selector, time_bounded, payload_filtered) (rate(control_plane_tenant_event_query_body_bytes_total{tenant=~\"$tenant\", selector=~\"$selector\"}[$__rate_interval]))"
        }
      ]
    },
